/E (Historically, ASC 410-30-35-9 created a rebuttable presumption that a recovery is not probable if the claim is subject to litigation. While the SCOTUS ruling has resolved the primary legal question, management must remain cautious. The prospect of new, restrictive regulations regarding refund procedures could actually make satisfying the "probable" threshold more difficult in the near term.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [10]
>>
